{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia","id":1064054,"title":"Malkovian Malkavia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-17T15:24:02-07:00","id":1064054,"title":"Malkovian Malkavia","content":"Hello friends!<br /> <br /> I did a google search just to see if this had been discussed before, and I found nothing. If it has been discussed at exhausting length, please link me to the former discussion.<br /> <br /> IF NOT, let's chat about it right now.<br /> <br /> How do you handle <i>The M</i>, the disease Malkavia, and the existence of the Malkovian bloodline? Both were obviously inspired by the Malkavians from VtM. As far as I see, there are a couple of ways to run it.<br /> <br /> 1) Malkavia originated from the Malkovians.<br /> 2) Malkavia has nothing to do with the Malkovians whatsoever. They are both callbacks to the Malkavians in VtM, but they are different enough in concept that they are simply unrelated.<br /> 3) We're just gonna pretend that the Malkovians don't exist. They were a weird, <i>weird </i>decision back in 2004 when VtR had no idea what direction it was going in. Malkavia is clearly the &quot;real&quot; descendant of the Malkavians.<br /> 4) Other<br /> <br /> Which do you usually do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T16:27:21-07:00","id":1064076,"title":"","content":"3 with a splash of 4. The 4 being that my version of Malkavia is effectively a contagious bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T19:54:54-07:00","id":1064150,"title":"","content":"1 and 4. The first Malkovian manifested a contagious mental disorder that, when passed on to a Ventrue without a bloodline, inducts him into the bloodline. Unqualified vampires and humans just get the disorders, without the ability to take advantage of it. <br /> <br /> And I'm sure I got this idea from a homebrew or something. Can't remember which, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:16:06-07:00","id":1064158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1064076#post1064076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 with a splash of 4. The 4 being that my version of Malkavia is effectively a contagious bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Malkavia (from the clan book) is already effectively a contagious bloodline by design. The only difference is that it doesn't fill a character's &quot;bloodline slot&quot;. It's also not clan exclusive, but that's not unique to Malkavia.<br /> Anyway, that's how I'd run it as well if I were to ST Vampire. I'd probably rework Dementation to better fit with 2E. Maybe make it a series of Devotions where the first is granted at &quot;induction&quot;. I'd have to think more about it.<br /> Malkovians could still be useful as a false lead if someone were to try to find the origin of Malkavia, but it would not be the true origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T22:42:13-07:00","id":1064191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1064158#post1064158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkavia (from the clan book) is already effectively a contagious bloodline by design. The only difference is that it doesn't fill a character's &amp;quot;bloodline slot&amp;quot;. It's also not clan exclusive, but that's not unique to Malkavia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my version is meant to capture the clanbook version fairly faithfully. It does take up your Bloodline &quot;slot&quot; in my version though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1064158#post1064158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, that's how I'd run it as well if I were to ST Vampire. I'd probably rework Dementation to better fit with 2E. Maybe make it a series of Devotions where the first is granted at &amp;quot;induction&amp;quot;. I'd have to think more about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I would (and do) completely scrap Dementation as a Discipline. The Malkavian Bloodline Gift in my version is more comparable to the Neglatu Gift, in that it's kind of a collection of things Malkavians can just <i>do</i>. Only while their symptoms are active, though. While the drawback is in remission, they lose access to the Gift.<br /> <br /> A draft of it is on the Homebrew Hub, though I have since made some tweaks to it, and I can no longer access that google doc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T04:04:40-07:00","id":1064249,"title":"","content":"At this point? To be honest, I feel like new!Nightmare with bits of Auspex captures the ideals of old Dementation in the first place. Maybe some tweaks, but I'm actually less comfortable using a vampire-madness-disease-as-bloodline now. Especially since it revolves around triggering &quot;derangements&quot; that we don't even have in the first place. The Delusional Condition fits that niche nicely, and its just a 3rd dot ability. I don't really think there's anything that's in Dementation that's worth keeping as a separate ability at this point. And that means there's really no benefit for it. &quot;Mad Insight&quot; into having some skill they shouldn't is easily represented by the Steadfast Condition, which is easy to get, especially with Lay Open the Mind or exceptional rolls on anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that Malk madness can't be a thing, but as a bloodline, I just don't feel it. I just don't feel like there is any benefit, and it undermines the horror of a disease / poison spreading. So, in my case, I just ignore the bloodline thing altogether. Both the original &quot;but we can do what Masquerade did!&quot; bloodline in the old core, and as a pseudo-one in the clan book. Malkavia is a disease vector that can infect vampires and twist them. Its a concern for unhealthy feeding practices and bad living. Something I'd do more along the lines of Morbus than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of the Morbus, I feel like there should be some kind of devotion or ability that all vampires have access to that deals with disease to some extent. *ponders some Animalism devotions to that effect?* Or maybe Cruac / Theban. Its definitely more fitting for divine punishment... sorry, I'll stop now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-18-2017, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T08:02:49-07:00","id":1064300,"title":"","content":"4. Malkovians exist, but the Malkavia disease does not. Malkovians have a bloodline gift that replicates some aspects of Dementation. And frequenly a codependent relationship with the Morotrophians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 03-21-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:55:47-07:00","id":1065899,"title":"","content":"2. When the existence of his Bloodline came to public attention, some wit simply noted the similarities between 'Malkavia' and 'Malkov', merged the two, and thus named the lineage with a truly awful pun. Malkov's opinion on the matter is unknown, but the namer of the line vanished shortly thereafter (but then, she was a Mekhet, so who can say?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:42:47-07:00","id":1066387,"title":"","content":"3. Not a fan of a lot of the legacy stuff from Masquerade but having it as a disease is interesting enough to warrant putting in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:07:59-07:00","id":1066590,"title":"","content":"It actually varies depending on the game I'm running. I mostly ignored the Malkovians even before Malkavia was a thing, and once it was I used it pretty much exclusively. Over time though I've found aspects of the Malkovians I like and have started using them more. I was/am a big player of Malkavians in VtM, and so like a lot of people I found the Malkovians very watered down and was much pleased when a more recognizable version appeared in the Ventrue clanbook. A lot of that is because I started playing VtM in Revised though, and that prototype of Malkavians is actually a somewhat different animal from the prototype they had in earlier editions. After having played a couple of more &quot;old school&quot; Malkavians I got a better understanding of the niche they operated in which in turn gave me better insight into what the real angle of the Malkovians was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:31:16-07:00","id":1066598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1066590#post1066590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of that is because I started playing VtM in Revised though, and that prototype of Malkavians is actually a somewhat different animal from the prototype they had in earlier editions. After having played a couple of more &quot;old school&quot; Malkavians I got a better understanding of the niche they operated in which in turn gave me better insight into what the real angle of the Malkovians was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really <i>love </i>this explanation, pointing out how Malkovians are more like the Dominate Malkavians and Malkavia is more like the Dementation Malkavians. That's <i>so awesome</i>!!!<br /> <br /> I'm actually playing a (really Demented, but I'm trying to be true-to-form and not Fish) Malkavian right now in my local Masquerade LARP, and there are definitely two different beasts between the &quot;Dominate&quot; family and the &quot;Dementation&quot; family.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T23:17:50-07:00","id":1066714,"title":"","content":"I have such a love/hate realtionship with Malkavians/Malkovians/Malkavia/etc. I love the idea of a Discipline or other supernatural power that functions like a disease. Hate the idea of a contagious mental illness. Love the idea of a Clan or Bloodline of seers, who's insight causes them to view the world differently and are often treated as &quot;mad&quot; because of it. Hate the idea of a Clan or Bloodline of &quot;crazy people&quot;. And these already conflicted feelings are only made more complicated by the fact that they're ultimately just Masquerade baggage.<br /> <br /> I think my ideal take on the whole thing would be in my hypothetical magical Christmasland Masquerade reboot setting. Malkavians would be a Clan of seers with Auspex, Obfuscate, and Dominate, with a weakness that had nothing to do with Derangements, and the madness thing would just be a stereotype based on their weird way of looking at the world. Dementation would be a disease, much like Requiem's Malkavia, that could be contracted by any vampire, one side-effect of which would be hallucinations. Antitribu Malkavians would have a reputation for intentionally exposing themselves to the disease so as to weaponize it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:14:54-07:00","id":1066929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1066714#post1066714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have such a love/hate realtionship with Malkavians/Malkovians/Malkavia/etc. I love the idea of a Discipline or other supernatural power that functions like a disease. Hate the idea of a contagious mental illness. Love the idea of a Clan or Bloodline of seers, who's insight causes them to view the world differently and are often treated as &quot;mad&quot; because of it. Hate the idea of a Clan or Bloodline of &quot;crazy people&quot;. And these already conflicted feelings are only made more complicated by the fact that they're ultimately just Masquerade baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fwiw, I've never seen the Malkavians as actually &quot;crazy.&quot; I've only ever played V20/V20 Dark Ages, but it's made pretty clear in both that the Malkavians' &quot;mental illness&quot; is not actually a &quot;mental illness&quot; at all (medication nor therapy will solve it) but the result of a shard of an ancient god being embedded in their minds. The sexy twenty-something's persona is totally overpowered by the ancient blood god, resulting in a three-way war between the neonate, their own Beast, and Malkav himself. Not to mention, <b>every other Malkavian who is or was </b>has a shard of this ancient blood god in their mind as well, and the shards are stretching out towards each other in an attempt to become whole again.<br /> <br /> The result? The vampire hears voices. The vampire suddenly knows things they shouldn't know. The vampire sees weird, chaotic &quot;hallucinations&quot; that they can only explain in the most bizarre terms. The vampire is extremely paranoid that something is coming after him because some Malkavian, somewhere, really is in danger. So other vampires, and even the Malkavians themselves who don't quite understand it, just say &quot;the Malkavians are totally off the wall nuts.&quot; But it's not that simple at all.<br /> <br /> It's possible that I might run Malkavia as being similar - a sentient virus that is overriding the influence of The Blood - or perhaps is merely a mutation of The Blood - and seeking to reproduce itself. But the difference between WoD and CofD is that the Malkavian thing above is <i>fact</i>, and the Malkavia option I just suggested is merely a <i>possibility. </i>...which is why I generally prefer CofD to WoD, but some people like having strict canon and that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:29:33-07:00","id":1066993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1066929#post1066929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fwiw, I've never seen the Malkavians as actually &amp;quot;crazy.&amp;quot; I've only ever played V20/V20 Dark Ages, but it's made pretty clear in both that the Malkavians' &amp;quot;mental illness&amp;quot; is not actually a &amp;quot;mental illness&amp;quot; at all (medication nor therapy will solve it) but the result of a shard of an ancient god being embedded in their minds. The sexy twenty-something's persona is totally overpowered by the ancient blood god, resulting in a three-way war between the neonate, their own Beast, and Malkav himself. Not to mention, <b>every other Malkavian who is or was </b>has a shard of this ancient blood god in their mind as well, and the shards are stretching out towards each other in an attempt to become whole again.<br /> <br /> The result? The vampire hears voices. The vampire suddenly knows things they shouldn't know. The vampire sees weird, chaotic &amp;quot;hallucinations&amp;quot; that they can only explain in the most bizarre terms. The vampire is extremely paranoid that something is coming after him because some Malkavian, somewhere, really is in danger. So other vampires, and even the Malkavians themselves who don't quite understand it, just say &amp;quot;the Malkavians are totally off the wall nuts.&amp;quot; But it's not that simple at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their portrayal seems to vary a lot from one edition to the next. The 20th Annoversary Editions really do their best to address the more problematic aspects of WoD, including Malkavians' madness. Making it simply an emergent property of the madness network is a decent band-aid. It's actually pretty similar to how I would portray them in my hypothetical reboot, but there are definitely example characters from earlier books who's Derangements really can't be explained by the madness network. Like the guy from Alien Hunger who literally thinks he's Jimmy Hendrix. Ultimately as long as their weakness is &quot;you have a Derrangement&quot; and Derangements are based on mental illnesses, no amount of hand-waving can really fix that underlying issue, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1066929#post1066929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible that I might run Malkavia as being similar - a sentient virus that is overriding the influence of The Blood - or perhaps is merely a mutation of The Blood - and seeking to reproduce itself. But the difference between WoD and CofD is that the Malkavian thing above is <i>fact</i>, and the Malkavia option I just suggested is merely a <i>possibility. </i>...which is why I generally prefer CofD to WoD, but some people like having strict canon and that's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. More mystery is another important thing I would want to include in a Masquerade reboot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:53:00-07:00","id":1067011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1066993#post1066993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately as long as their weakness is &quot;you have a Derrangement&quot; and Derangements are based on mental illnesses, no amount of hand-waving can really fix that underlying issue, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. A big part of the problem is that Derangements are not now and have never been a well executed game element in any iteration of the WoD. Some of them are attempting to portray real mental illnesses, others more sensational forms of madness from media and literature, others are specific supernatural conditions, and none of them have consistent mechanical or role-play representation. Something that I have tried to emphasize when I use Malkavians (in either Masquerade or Requiem) is that madness =/= mental illness. I'm only one person though, and that isn't going to stop others from conflating the concepts. Nor does it remove the DNA they still have from their earliest inception in which the two were obviously and clearly conflated by the authors both in terms of story and rules. Nor does it remove the prominent and awkward role that &quot;madness&quot; plays in the gothic literature that informs Vampire and the cultural moment that birthed it. Nor indeed does it stop a lot of so-called &quot;good&quot; Malkavian players from using fish-wielding cartoon characters as their only metric of comparison against their own behavior and continuing to fetishize mental illness through roleplay they persistently believe to be somehow elevated. <br /> <br /> That rant being said, I still love Malkavians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:08:02-07:00","id":1067019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1067011#post1067011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That rant being said, I still love Malkavians.</div> </div> </div> </div>problematic faves are a thing. I hate to admit it, but I actually <i>do </i>love the Ravnos as they are presented in V20/Dark Ages, but damn is it impossible to separate them from their super racist past. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:11:31-07:00","id":1067374,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing they just get the Madness condition in 2e which I think cleans up the derangement problem. Personally, I think the condition as the Malkavian curse would be pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> Ravnos in the Dark Ages is not so much the problem as they would have been con artists and horse thieves. I think the assumption that a culture remains unchanged after hundreds of years despite evidence to the contrary is where the fail comes in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 03-24-2017, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:09:11-07:00","id":1067595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1067374#post1067374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing they just get the Madness condition in 2e which I think cleans up the derangement problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. It's a step in the right direction from Derangements, but it's still a Clan/Bloodline/whatever defined by &quot;madness.&quot; If their eccentricities are supposed to be the result of their future vision making them see the world differently, or their hive mind causing invasive thoughts, or their Clan/Bloodline culture having particularly alien values, then that should be explicitly stated and the mechanics should reflect it. If you just slap them with the Madness Condition and call it a day you're not really addressing the underlying issue.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, if you're going to boil Malkavian &quot;madness&quot; down to a Condition, a more appropriate one would be Primeval Truths. Give them that every time they have a prophetic vision or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-24-2017, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:55:21-07:00","id":1067620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1067595#post1067595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, if you're going to boil Malkavian &quot;madness&quot; down to a Condition, a more appropriate one would be Primeval Truths. Give them that every time they have a prophetic vision or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which game is Primeval Truths in? Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:38:08-07:00","id":1067648,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants for Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:18:13-07:00","id":1067664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1064054-malkovian-malkavia?p=1067648#post1067648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secrets of the Covenants for Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. I actually physically own that book. I should know that....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:37:26-07:00","id":1067794,"title":"","content":"I like the mechanics of the Madness condition. I don't care about the fluff as that should be modified to fit Malkavians. Negative dice based on Humanity that occasionally work against mental or social rolls represents a mind that is distracted or knows too much. I think that obviously beats out welcome to the Malkavian line here is your OCD, or whatever. I don't care as much for the mechanics of Primeval Truths as a clan/bloodline curse. It would require more work because I don't think never gaining willpower is a viable option. Perhaps I was unclear when I said they would get the condition. I don't mean that literally because the condition can go away. Malkavians would never be able to remove the condition, hence the occasional penalties seems like an interesting experience as far as curses go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:40:10-07:00","id":1070271,"title":"","content":"Personally I feel that that the shift in focus of Malkavians/Malkovians from being a clan of &quot;madness&quot; to being a clan of &quot;seers&quot; creates more problems than it solves. The main thing is how much narrower that theme is. It creates a dichotomy where you're either a prophet or a fish-malk. Your psychological or neurological status is only tolerated as long as it also gives you an exploitable superpower. A clan of &quot;seers&quot; also has a much thinner strata of individuals who would meet their criteria for embrace, whereas I've always felt one of the interesting aspects of Malkavians as a clan is that you could really come from just about any background or walk of life. I also find that &quot;madness&quot; offers an opportunity to explore the ways that various forms of mental illness, neuroatypicality, and even social nonconformity have been grappled with across cultures and time periods. &quot;Seers&quot; don't really do the same. <br /> <br /> Is &quot;madness&quot; problematic? Yeah. My preference is to deal with it head on though rather than shunting the focus sideways into what is really a mechanical rather than a thematic role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T18:21:23-07:00","id":1070414,"title":"","content":"I keep both iterations and expand upon the origin mythos in Lords of the Damned involving Lord Nicholas of the Polaskis and the mysterious Malkav. It's mentioned that Lord Nicholas had two ghouls, one who gets embraced by Malkav and the other dying of vitae starvation following Malkav's escape. The former supposedly resides in London. I use that Ghoul as the origin point of the Malkovian bloodline.<br /> <br /> The idea being that he contracted Malkavia and through his own efforts found a stopgap cure by forging a Bloodline - not so much doing away with the condition as stabilizing it. Members of the bloodline no longer act as a vector, thus allowing them to interact with Malkavians without worry of spreading it. Malkovians derive their name from an attempt to distinguish the metaphorical strains, but it's lost on most Kindred. If I'm using them in a chronicle I give them a few bloodline specific devotions and merits that allow them to shepherd the Malkavians, calming their minds momentarily and providing a resistance to some of the nastier products of Dementation.<br /> <br /> It's a victory of a sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:19:39-07:00","id":1070654,"title":"","content":"My version of Malkavian are a bloodline/clan related to the Mekhet, and hold the &quot;odd seer&quot; place in Kindred society thanks to exposing their minds to supernatural forces and beings outside time and space. So yes, Lovecraftian influence. All in all, it's not a new approach, I just needed to file the serial numbers off and fit them in usefully.<br /> <br /> And they can embrace anyone they feel &quot;called&quot; to--usually because said person exhibits some weird way of looking at the world, not because they are already mad or see visions. The visions? Those will come.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}